      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Research indicates that the SAT score gap is influenced by a complex interplay of socioeconomic factors, not solely on inherent ability. Key contributors include disparities in educational resources, such as unequal access to high-quality schools and AP courses, for different racial groups. Additionally, differences in family income and the resources available at home significantly impact test preparation and academic support. These systemic issues create an unequal starting line for students before they even take the exam.",
